  "notes": "USAGE:\n{固辞|こじ} implies a strong, unwavering refusal. It is often used when someone declines a position, honor, payment, or other offer that others think they should accept.\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {固辞|こじ}する (to firmly decline)\n- {申|もう}し{出|で}を{固辞|こじ}する (to firmly decline an offer)\n- {役職|やくしょく}を{固辞|こじ}する (to firmly decline a position)\n\nSIMILAR WORDS:\n{辞退|じたい} means to decline or withdraw (e.g., from a position or competition) and is less emphatic. {固辞|こじ} stresses the firmness and persistence of the refusal.",
